{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-glossary-descent","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:glossary-descent","kind":"remark","title":"Descent","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-qu-to-qou"],"tags":["glossary","descent","brane-tower","restriction"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.DescentData","text":"glossary-descent.md","leanSource":"glossary-descent.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:glossary-descent\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{A_n\\}_{n \\geq 0}</code> be the recursive brane tower. The <strong><a class=\"refterm\" href=\"#term-descent\">descent</a></strong> is the reverse traversal of the tower. Passage from level <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code> to level <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n{-}1</code> applies the restriction morphism <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r_n \\colon A_n = J^1(A_{n-1}) \\to A_{n-1}</code>. In the archimedean realisation, this restricts the connection and bundle to the base manifold <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">M_{n-1}</code>. The descent terminates in finitely many steps, bounded by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Krulldim} Z(\\mathrm{End}_{\\mathbf{C}}(A))</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/notation/glossary-descent.md","heading":"Remark","number":"30.3.5","page":"b/rem-glossary-descent","qa":{"counts":{"pass":71,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":8,"unknown":0,"stale":62},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.DescentData","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/notation/glossary-descent.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
